CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness 
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
The same program as thread_private_object on the default path, i.e. with the
per-round chain, since --thread-private is off by default.
The two encodings have to agree; this is the arm that says so.

 also reproduces the pre-change formula to the digit on the
benchmark the change was measured on (28-race_reach_81-list_racing u2 r8:
123237 variables, 424544 clauses either way), so it doubles as the control
showing the change is confined to the private path.
